<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to October 30 as released by the Bank of Japan on Thursday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.38 (0.39)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.47 (0.50)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  1.00 (1.04)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.33 (0.34)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.42 (0.45)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.95 (0.99)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.29 (0.30)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.37 (0.40)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.26)	 three years  0.90 (0.94)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Oct 28 - Nov 01:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.48 (0.50)   120-150 days  0.52 (0.54)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.50 (0.50)   150-180 days  0.55 (0.54)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.50 (0.51)   180-360 days  0.55 (0.57)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.52 (0.53)   over 360 days 0.62 (UNQ )</p>
